# Mutation cases for "a byte string crosses a `<param>` and a `<donedata>` as its
# byte-exact Latin-1 text" under the Rust backend
# (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15, "A byte string"; docs/adr/0005, decision 2).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_static_rust_bytes_cross_a_param_as_their_latin1_text_rust.cases`.
#
# `static_bytes_wire` keeps the bytes the host raised, sends them to itself as the
# `<param>` of `framed.relayed`, reads that event's payload back into `echo`, and finishes
# with `echo` in a `<donedata>`. The bytes include some above 0x7F, a quote, a backslash
# and a control byte, so the text has to be the character of each byte and not the bytes
# decoded as UTF-8. The mutant takes that decision away:
#
#   a byte slice crosses as its UTF-8 decoding, which replaces what is not UTF-8.
#
# A mutant that refused the `<param>` is no case here: the regeneration skips a document a
# language refuses, and would leave the machine it generated before standing.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_tests -p sce-rust-tests --test static_scenarios --test static_datamodel
mutation_targets sce-build/src/forge/static_lowering.rs
mutation_targets backends/rust/tests/src/integration/static_datamodel/static_bytes_wire_sm.rs
mutation_regen scripts/regen_static_datamodel_rust.sh
mutation_oracles backends/rust/tests/tests/static_scenarios.rs sce-build/tests/fixtures/static_datamodel/scenarios/static_bytes_wire.json

mutation_case "a byte slice crosses as its UTF-8 decoding" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/src/forge/static_lowering.rs",
     "            &format!(\"::sce_rust_runtime::event_payload::bytes_as_payload_text(&{value})\"),",
     "            &format!(\"String::from_utf8_lossy(&{value}).into_owned()\"),")
PY
